#!/usr/bin/env etcs
#IMPORT ACE_ROOT/modules

# Server-side TLS termination, minimal. Run it directly -- nothing here
# blocks, so the trace completes and hands the shell straight back while the
# gate keeps running. The server outlives this script because the ENTITY
# holds the accept scope, not because the trace is still executing.
#
# For the full site over TLS -- landing page, file tree, chess and forum
# lobbies -- see run_tls_website.etcs. This file is the smoke test: the
# smallest trace that proves termination works, plus the checks worth
# running against it.
#
# The point of this trace is what it DOESN'T say. There is exactly one TLS
# line in it. The page, the tree and the routing are byte-identical to
# run_website.etcs -- HttpServer::Serve and every other subscriber keep
# receiving plaintext and never learn a handshake happened. If serving a
# page over TLS required teaching the page about TLS, the change would be
# in the wrong layer.
#
# Generate a self-signed cert first. The -addext line is not optional
# padding: without a subjectAltName, modern clients reject the cert on
# hostname grounds ALONE, before ever considering the issuer -- which would
# make check 3 below pass for the wrong reason.
#
#   openssl req -x509 -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -days 30 \
#     -keyout /tmp/etcs-key.pem -out /tmp/etcs-cert.pem \
#     -subj "/CN=localhost" \
#     -addext "subjectAltName=DNS:localhost,IP:127.0.0.1"
#
# OpenSSL 3.x writes the key as PKCS#8 ("BEGIN PRIVATE KEY"), which
# mbedtls_pk_parse_keyfile reads without help.

spawn NetworkProvider::HttpServer web
web.SetPort(8443)

# BEFORE Start, and that is load-bearing rather than stylistic. Start mints
# the ConnectionManager and Opens it in one step, and Open begins accepting
# immediately -- so there is no later point in this trace at which the gate
# exists but has not yet taken a connection. Enabling TLS afterwards would
# always race the first client. This line only stores the paths; Start is
# what hands them to the gate, and Start REFUSES to come up if either file
# fails to load rather than falling back to plaintext on a port that was
# asked to be TLS.
web.EnableTLS(/tmp/etcs-cert.pem, /tmp/etcs-key.pem)

web.spawn(NetworkProvider::StaticHtmlPage landing)
landing.SetHtmlFromFile(./www/index.html)

web.spawn(NetworkProvider::FileHtmlPage tree)
tree.LoadFromDisk(./www)
tree.ListPaths()

web.Start()
web.IsStarted()